  "description": "Pilkington float glass process: molten glass poured onto a bath of molten tin at ~1000°C in a controlled nitrogen/hydrogen atmosphere, producing perfectly flat, parallel-surface glass ribbon without grinding or polishing. Accounts for >90% of worldwide flat glass production for windows, mirrors, and architectural glazing.",
